{"kind":"request","text":"Repair the documentation pages that rest on retired artifacts, so they can flare again when the behaviour they describe moves.\n\nFour pages cite an artifact the fold has retired: docs/concepts/work-loop.md and docs/reference/gs/review.md both name 7bf40860 at cmd/gs/main.go; docs/how-to/deploy-a-resident.md names a13f26c1 at spike/internal/app; docs/reference/gs/serve.md names both a13f26c1 and ec925bb7 at spike/cmd/gs. Five retired anchors across four pages.\n\nA retired artifact has already been superseded, so its flare has fired and no future one will: later work at that path supersedes the live artifact instead, and a page anchored to the retired one never hears about it. Each page keeps looking anchored while being permanently deaf to the area its anchor named.\n\nTwo of the five cannot be repaired at the same path. spike/cmd/gs and spike/internal/app have no live artifact, because the code left those paths in the spike-to-main migration; the successors are at cmd/gs and internal/app. That is the rename case AGENTS.md describes: re-anchor to wherever the behaviour now lives.\n\nThis replaces an earlier attempt at e9a1c55a that codex reviewed and refused on two grounds, both correct. It carried no request or promise, resting on an assert, and AGENTS.md exempts self-initiated work only when the implementing commit rests on a motivating ratified decision, which an assert is not. And its internal/app selection justified 72e8adfd on the grounds that ca1decfc at 83e60c30 was not in main; 83e60c30 has since merged as 63d8d765 and 845e3cc9 is the stable current artifact, so that rationale would have been false on landing.","body":{"conditions":"No page under docs/ names a retired artifact in its rests_on; each replacement is the live, non-stale artifact at the path the behaviour now lives at, choosing the later in-main artifact where two are in main; the unchanged prose on each repaired page is checked against the behaviour present in the selected artifact commits rather than assumed; the docset gates pass including the executable examples; and the head is zero commits behind main and merges clean, with an exact-head review by a different actor before merge","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}